d polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Michigan sits at the center of the electoral map, with an even partisan lean and a history of deciding presidential elections by razor-thin margins. The incumbent president is term-limited, so both parties will nominate fresh candidates with no incumbency advantage on either side. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, and no fundraising figures have been reported for either campaign.\n\nHeadline coverage so far focuses on Democratic primary politics, including the state's early primary slot and a competitive Senate race, rather than the fall general election, providing little signal about how the matchup will develop. With fundamentals dead even and no other evidence to weigh, the race stands as a pure tossup, and uncertainty should stay wide until real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4963, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5203, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4949, "margin": 0.0}]}